    "outcomeVariants": {
      "solid": [
        "By the end of the season it is no longer the first thing you think about when a free morning appears.",
        "Nothing about it worsens over the season, and it stops being the item that makes you flinch at the calendar.",
        "The trip in July happens and the double shift in August happens, and neither of them has to be arranged around it.",
        "The paperwork about it goes from the top of the pile into a drawer and stays in the drawer. Nothing this season puts it back on the counter.",
        "Your aunt asks about it once in September and the answer takes one sentence. In the spring it would have taken most of the call."
      ],
      "mixed": [
        "It is neither resolved nor ignored. The season ends with it still open and better understood than it was.",
        "Progress of the tedious sort. Nothing about it is finished and nothing about it is worse.",
        "You end the season with the same item on the list and a clearer idea of what taking it off will cost.",
        "It takes about as much out of the season as it gives back. The two other things you meant to get to this year are exactly where they were in April.",
        "Three separate times this season you think you have finished thinking about it, and three separate times it comes back up. By September it has stopped being urgent and has not stopped being there."
      ],
      "poor": [
        "The season ends with the item still on the list, and the time you put into it is not coming back.",
        "It stops waiting for you. What you deal with in a bad week costs more than what a quiet week would have cost.",
        "By August you have a way around it — the side you chew on, the light you read by — and you have stopped noticing that you are doing it.",
        "The referral from last year runs out in July, and getting another one means going back to the start of a line you were already in.",
        "It starts costing you elsewhere — the sleep, the Saturday you said no to, the errand you got somebody else to run. By September you are paying for it in places that have nothing to do with it."
      ]
    },
